.TH CWE-330 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-330 \- Use of Insufficiently Random Values
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The product uses insufficiently random numbers or values in a security context that depends on unpredictable numbers. When product generates predictable values in a context requiring unpredictability, it may be possible for an attacker to guess the next value that will be generated, and use this guess to impersonate another user or access sensitive information.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB1\fR exploited CVE mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2020\-1472
Microsoft Netlogon, added 2021\-11\-03, ransomware: Known.
.PP
Microsoft Netlogon Privilege Escalation Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Microsoft's Netlogon Remote Protocol (MS\-NRPC) contains a privilege escalation vulnerability when an attacker establishes a vulnerable Netlogon secure channel connection to a domain controller. An attacker who successfully exploits the vulnerability could run a specially crafted application on a device on the network. The vulnerability is also known under the moniker of Zerologon.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2022\-05\-03.
.PP
\fIReferences:\fR
.br
https://www.cisa.gov/news\-events/directives/ed\-20\-04\-mitigate\-netlogon\-elevation\-privilege\-vulnerability\-august\-2020\-patch\-tuesday
.br
https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE\-2020\-1472
.SH EXAMPLES
One vulnerable\->fixed pair per ecosystem (Python).
.SS Python
\fIVulnerable:\fR
.RS
.EX
import random
token = "%030x" % random.randrange(16**30)   # predictable PRNG
.EE
.RE
\fIFixed:\fR
.RS
.EX
import secrets
token = secrets.token_hex(16)                # CSPRNG
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
